    "notes": "Delay-reason tally kept alongside the wait-time sampling, same 10 weekday mornings (2026-07-20 to 2026-07-31). Tally rule agreed on day one: one tap when a sampled order's handoff is visibly held up by the named cause -- the dominant cause per order, not every cause. Categories were set up front from the July 15 pre-study walk; timestamps are the POS wall clock (local). Exported with to_dataset and run through the engine Pareto -- drink-queue backlog and grinder rework are the vital few at exactly 80% cumulative. Named for where the delay actually sits (six marked cups deep before the first pull, per E01's note) -- it is the drink queue at the espresso station backing up, not the register line.",
